// What still collides once two bindings of the same declaration do not.
//
// Name-resolution stage. A name reached by two routes is one binding only where
// both routes reach the same declaration the same way. Two declarations that
// happen to share a spelling collide exactly as before, and so does one member
// folded through two different globals, since each is reached through its own.
//
// The folder holds:
//   c1/c1.cone   declares x
//   c2/c2.cone   declares another x
//   a/a.cone     re-exports c1's names
//   b/b.cone     re-exports c2's names
//   d/d.cone     wildcard-imports a and b: two x's, one name
//   g/g.cone     folds one member through two globals of one type

fn reach() i64 {
  d.y();
}
